1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:01,495
Why ‘a lot
of knowledge’,

2
00:00:01,535 --> 00:00:03,048
but ‘three ideas’?

3
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,915
He knows many
facts about art.

4
00:00:05,955 --> 00:00:07,650
But knowledge names
his whole body

5
00:00:07,690 --> 00:00:08,653
of understanding,

6
00:00:08,693 --> 00:00:10,296
not each fact
separately.

7
00:00:10,336 --> 00:00:12,008
So not ‘many
knowledges’.

8
00:00:12,537 --> 00:00:12,945
Say:

9
00:00:12,985 --> 00:00:15,075
‘He has a lot
of knowledge about art.’

10
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:16,845
Advice works
similarly:

11
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:17,602
‘some advice’,

12
00:00:17,642 --> 00:00:20,183
or count it as ‘two
pieces of advice’.

13
00:00:21,103 --> 00:00:22,935
But an idea
is abstract too,

14
00:00:22,975 --> 00:00:25,048
and ‘three ideas’
is correct.

15
00:00:25,088 --> 00:00:27,095
Abstract doesn’t
decide it.

16
00:00:27,135 --> 00:00:27,791
Ask:

17
00:00:27,831 --> 00:00:29,453
does this word
name one undivided

18
00:00:29,493 --> 00:00:31,629
body,
or separate items?

